`program_needed` is true, false, or null. Null is not in the unneeded-program rate. Chat and the trick
questions that need no computation are false. Decimals, fractions, the square root, and the 1-to-100 sum are
null. Follow-ups are null.

## Scoring

The answer region is `reason_loop.answer_region`: text after the last `</final>` or `</think>`, then the last
`Answer:` line inside that tail when one is present. A value that appears only inside `<final>` is not the
answer. `daudit_score.answer_region` is checked equal to REASON's on three samples.

Correctness is rule-based. `needs_human` items have `answer_match` null. Accuracy uses items with status
`ok` and `needs_human` false. `not_run`, `over_context`, and `error` are coverage gaps, not wrong answers.
A `time_cap` item is status `ok` when the loop returned text, and that text is scored.

| kind | match |
| --- | --- |
| int | last integer in the region. Decimals are removed first, so 3.75 does not yield 75. Commas inside a number are dropped. A leading unicode minus is a hyphen. |
| decimal | last decimal, `Decimal` equality |
| fraction | last fraction, equal as a rational, or a decimal equal to that rational |
| fraction_lowest | the printed fraction must already be in lowest terms. 2/4 does not match 1/2 |
| yesno, bool, choice | the option whose match starts latest. The boundary is not a word character and not a dot, so 0.9 does not match inside 0.90 and "no" does not match inside "north" |
| pair | the last `(x, y)`, or the last `x=` together with the last `y=` |
| cents | decimal 0.05, or the words "5 cents" or "five cents". A bare 5 does not match |
| noah | "noah", or none / zero / 0 / "no animals" |
| undef | undefined, not defined, does not exist, infinity, infinite, divide by zero, division by zero |
| hello, sky, word, h2o | the word, with `H2O` allowing spaces (`h 2 o`) |
| human | no rule. `answer_match` is null |

`recompute` parses the question and does not read `reference`. The generator does not call it. The check
requires them to agree on every scored item that is not a follow-up. Follow-up references copy the stem.
Subtraction references are computed from the two integers in the generator, not from `recompute`.

A program counts as written when the transcript contains `<program>` or the clock recorded a call.
The unneeded-program rate is that flag among status-`ok` items whose `program_needed` is false, within the
category. Null is outside the rate.

Times are nearest-rank percentiles of `wall_s` on status-`ok` items. Rank is `max(1, ceil(p/100 * n))`,
1-based into the sorted list. The table reports the median and the 90th percentile.

Cause labels, assigned after the transcripts are read, are only: compile, table, quote, glue, wrong decision
to compute, format, speed. The guess maps onto the plan: library adder plus parallel scan, name allocation,
reading input in place, an independent BigInt answer check, judgment on when to compute, DAgger repairs,
phrasing diversity, language gates. `daudit_summarize.py` prints a first label from the call errors. That
label is not the ranking.

## What a record contains

One JSON line per attempt, last line per id wins: id, category, family, status, needs_human, program_needed,
reference, follow_of, answer_match, detail, got, the full transcript, program_written, certificate verdict,
n_calls, n_errors, ticks, tokens generated, wall_s, finish, and a slim call list (error, certified, ticks,
value, the first 800 characters of the program).

Certificate verdicts: `no_program`, `error`, `passed`, `failed`, `mixed`, `no_run`. Base records say
`no_clock`.

## Run order

Length bucket (under 500 characters, under 3,000, else), then category, then id. A follow-up runs immediately
after its stem. Short items cover every category if the job clock hits. The 4,096-digit items and the
1,000-swap item are in the long bucket and run last. The longest prompts at registration fit: the 1,000-swap
question is 7,252 tokens and the 4,096-digit prompts are 8,210, under 40,960.

`--resume` copies an existing `records.jsonl` and skips ids whose last status is `ok`, `over_context`, or
`error`. `not_run` is retried.

